Requirements
============

To compile PokerTH, you need the following libraries:

- Qt version >= 6.7.0, 6.9.2 LTS recommended  --> https://www.qt.io/
- libboost_thread, libboost_filesystem, libboost_datetime, libboost_program_options,
  libboost_iostreams, libboost_asio, libboost_regex, libboost_random, libboost_uuid
  (version >= 1.83; the latest version is recommended)  --> http://www.boost.org/
- protoc >= 2.3.0 (during build), libprotobuf >= 2.3.0 -> https://github.com/google/protobuf
- OpenSSL

Basic Installation
==================

Linux:

  Type "cd path/to/the/sources". Then type:

  0. For a clean build and to test the binaries without installing, run:
    `bash clean_build.sh`. This cleans up the build directory and copies the
    TLS certificate and data directory into it.

  1. Type `cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE:STRING=Release -S. -B./build -G Ninja`

  2. Type `cmake --build ./build --config Release --target all --` to compile all targets.
      ... you can specify the following binary build targets instead:
      `pokerth_qml-client` (the current client), `pokerth_client` (the classic Qt Widgets client),
      `pokerth_dedicated_server`, `pokerth_official_server`, `pokerth_chatcleaner`

  3. Become root by typing "su" or "sudo -s", then run:
      `cmake --install ./build`

Windows:
see ./docker/windows folder

Android:
see ./docker/android/README_android.md

MacOS:
see ./build_macos_combined.sh (both clients), ./build_macos_qml.sh, ./build_macos_widget.sh

iOS:
see ./build_ios_qml.sh

All release builds also exist as manually triggered GitHub Actions workflows
in ./.github/workflows.
